1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,560
[Disclaimer: Characters, behaviors,
places, organizations, professions,

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:05,040
and events shown
in the series are entirely fictional,

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:07,520
solely for the purpose of entertainment,
with no intention to instruct

4
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:10,000
or promote any kind of behavior;
viewer discretion is advised]

5
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:11,170
I don't understand

6
00:00:11,190 --> 00:00:13,520
why a feng shui master like you
needs to change the house plans.

7
00:00:13,710 --> 00:00:14,910
So let's meet halfway.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,880
Whatever you can change,

9
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:18,380
go ahead and do it.

10
00:00:18,790 --> 00:00:19,790
Okay.

11
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,710
We won't have to see each other again.

12
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:26,400
Green is a lucky color.

13
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:29,840
Maybe you should carry something
that isn't bad luck for once.

14
00:00:29,990 --> 00:00:31,800
Why did you bring me here?

15
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:32,720
Scared?

16
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,280
Why should I be scared?

17
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:35,680
If you aren't scared,

18
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:36,990
then let's head inside.

19
00:00:37,290 --> 00:00:39,080
Are you Soul's girlfriend?

20
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,320
She's not my girlfriend, Mom.

21
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:45,440
Yes.

22
00:00:48,180 --> 00:00:48,690
So?

23
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,920
Yes or no?

24
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:52,300
- No!
- No!

25
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,120
No, I'm not.

26
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,760
I'm not her girlfriend.

27
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,600
I'm just the feng shui master

28
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:00,680
who works with Miss Architect.

29
00:01:00,890 --> 00:01:02,500
Oh.

30
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:03,920
I see.

31
00:01:04,210 --> 00:01:06,900
I've never seen
Soul bring anyone home before,

32
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,250
so I think you're...

33
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:09,000
Mom!

34
00:01:28,590 --> 00:01:29,900
Finally.

35
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:34,600
I'd better hurry back.

36
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:36,220
It's going to rain.

37
00:01:40,210 --> 00:01:41,700
I can give you a ride.

38
00:01:41,940 --> 00:01:43,390
My car has a roof, you know.

39
00:01:44,770 --> 00:01:45,770
Hey,

40
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:48,510
I just don't like rain.

41
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:06,620
Why won't you let me
drop you off at your house?

42
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:10,200
I don't want to answer my mom's questions.

43
00:02:10,220 --> 00:02:11,510
She'll keep asking,

44
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:13,720
"Why don't you take a taxi?"

45
00:02:13,810 --> 00:02:15,010
"Who is that?"

46
00:02:15,410 --> 00:02:16,600
"So, you have someone..."

47
00:02:18,110 --> 00:02:19,290
Are all moms like this,

48
00:02:19,310 --> 00:02:20,880
always nagging?

49
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:22,960
Did...

50
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:25,200
you just laugh?

51
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:28,560
Ahem.

52
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:29,980
No...

53
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:31,050
Ahem!

54
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,190
Here.

55
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,220
This is your payment.

56
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:40,000
I don't want it.

57
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,600
Just like we agreed.

58
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:44,760
But the ride here

59
00:02:44,890 --> 00:02:47,000
wasn't part of the deal either.

60
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,220
I don't want to hear my mom nagging

61
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:52,300
about why I let you go home alone.

62
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:53,780
Here.

63
00:02:54,460 --> 00:02:55,850
Then I'll consider

64
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,920
the dinner your mom made

65
00:02:58,190 --> 00:02:58,910
and

66
00:02:59,130 --> 00:03:00,300
this delicious cake

67
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:02,500
as my payment,

68
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,540
so we won't owe
each other anything anymore.

69
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,280
Don't come asking me to pay you, then.

70
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,120
I won't.

71
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:13,920
Good luck with Madam Waen's project.

72
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:17,040
If you want your work to go smoothly,

73
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:21,200
try wearing the day's lucky color.

74
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:24,370
Nonsense.

75
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:27,130
Suit yourself.

76
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,200
I'm leaving.

77
00:03:39,990 --> 00:03:41,600
I hope we don't see each other again,

78
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,200
Miss Architect.

79
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:51,760
Xinxin, you're back, dear?

80
00:05:56,900 --> 00:05:58,840
Whose car is that?

81
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:03,900
That's...

82
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:07,190
That's your car, dear.

83
00:06:07,510 --> 00:06:09,300
Well, Dad was worried that

84
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:11,700
you've been working late,

85
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,680
so he...

86
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:15,210
wanted you to have a car.

87
00:06:15,570 --> 00:06:16,810
So he bought it for you.

88
00:06:18,180 --> 00:06:19,560
But if you don't want it,

89
00:06:19,590 --> 00:06:20,720
- it's alright...
- I'll take it.

90
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:24,480
What do you mean, dear?

91
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:27,720
I’ll take it because it’s what I deserve.

92
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,400
It's only right that
he takes responsibility.

93
00:06:31,290 --> 00:06:33,000
But I'm not going to use it.

94
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:35,120
I'm going to sell it

95
00:06:35,140 --> 00:06:36,710
and keep the money.

96
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,080
[Korawitsueksa:
Father's Day, December 5th]

97
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:33,700
Mom.

98
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:34,720
Yes?

99
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:36,970
Mom,

100
00:07:36,990 --> 00:07:38,840
when will Dad come?

101
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:46,510
Xinxin, my dear.

102
00:07:47,580 --> 00:07:49,410
Dad is busy today.

103
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:51,510
He has work to do,

104
00:07:52,110 --> 00:07:54,560
so let me take his place for now, alright?

105
00:07:56,720 --> 00:07:57,720
But...

106
00:07:58,850 --> 00:08:01,900
my friends' dads were
able to make it, though.

107
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,120
Dad is really busy today, dear.

108
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:13,720
Come on.

109
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:30,080
Did you drop her off safely, dear?

110
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:32,300
Whoa, Mom, you scared me.

111
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:34,280
What's there to be scared of?

112
00:09:34,470 --> 00:09:35,910
So, how was it?

113
00:09:36,400 --> 00:09:38,230
I dropped her off safely,

114
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,760
just like you told me to.

115
00:09:41,590 --> 00:09:42,320
Hey,

116
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,780
you're really not Xinxin's girlfriend?

117
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:46,920
Mom!

118
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:50,160
I'm not dating every single woman
who happens to be around me.

119
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:54,880
I think there's something between you two...

120
00:09:55,980 --> 00:09:57,760
Something wrong, you mean.

121
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:02,040
If you two didn't get along,
why did you bring her home?

122
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:05,170
Didn't you say
a feng shui master and an architect

123
00:10:05,190 --> 00:10:06,560
are the perfect rivals?

124
00:10:07,780 --> 00:10:10,490
Well, if I'm the one watching this match,

125
00:10:10,690 --> 00:10:12,280
I'm definitely rooting for these two.

126
00:10:12,530 --> 00:10:13,710
Mom!

127
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:18,560
I think next time

128
00:10:18,810 --> 00:10:21,810
we should invite her over for dinner.

129
00:10:22,180 --> 00:10:23,640
I think she's lovely.

130
00:10:23,710 --> 00:10:24,910
I like her.

131
00:10:26,010 --> 00:10:26,760
Mom.

132
00:10:27,010 --> 00:10:29,040
Whatever you're hoping for,

133
00:10:29,330 --> 00:10:30,800
you can give up on it now.

134
00:10:31,410 --> 00:10:34,040
Because I'm not ready
to let anyone in right now.

135
00:11:12,510 --> 00:11:14,900
"How long are you going
to keep shutting yourself off?"

136
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,520
"Does one heartbreak

137
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:22,200
really make you scared to love again?"

138
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,480
"This cake is so good!"

139
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:04,900
Can I take some home with me?

140
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,940
[Lucky Colors 2026:
Never miss a beat when you dress right]

141
00:12:29,960 --> 00:12:32,390
"If you want your work to go smoothly,

142
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:35,120
try wearing the day's lucky color."

143
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:37,410
If the project goes smoothly,

144
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:38,920
it's because of skill,

145
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,600
not the color.

146
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,680
Or is it?

147
00:12:47,800 --> 00:12:48,800
Gosh.

148
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,080
[JR CONSTRUCTION]

149
00:12:57,730 --> 00:13:00,400
I’m thinking of renovating
a house into an office.

150
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:03,210
But I don't want it to
feel too strictly corporate.

151
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:06,680
I want it to feel homey
when they come to work.

152
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,610
Maybe we should remove this wall section,

153
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,510
so it will be more open

154
00:13:12,530 --> 00:13:13,930
and easier to see each other.

155
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:15,600
Mm...

156
00:13:15,630 --> 00:13:19,010
But I want my employees
to have more privacy.

157
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
Mm.

158
00:13:23,510 --> 00:13:26,010
They say people who don't like open spaces

159
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,200
are usually great at their jobs.

160
00:13:29,420 --> 00:13:32,200
Maybe they just don't want
to be watched all the time.

161
00:13:32,710 --> 00:13:33,710
I see.

162
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,680
Then let's...

163
00:13:35,710 --> 00:13:38,600
make this wall area more open

164
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:40,420
so people can still see each other,

165
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:41,510
but not too clearly.

166
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,200
Ms. Mim,

167
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:45,640
you can always disagree with me.

168
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:48,440
I don't know much about this anyway.

169
00:13:48,530 --> 00:13:50,400
Maybe something I said

170
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:51,610
won't actually work out.

171
00:13:52,950 --> 00:13:55,620
We don't design things just to
win arguments with our clients.

172
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:58,160
We design according to
what our clients want.

173
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:02,060
Do you do this for every client?

174
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,790
Only for a client who...

175
00:14:05,040 --> 00:14:06,890
doesn't need too much explanation,

176
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:09,090
is easy to work with,
and gets it right away.

177
00:14:10,310 --> 00:14:11,720
I like this type of client.

178
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,360
Let's get back to the project.

179
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:27,360
I haven't even gotten off-topic yet.

180
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:31,480
I'll draft the zoning plan
and a rough concept,

181
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:33,080
then I'll email them to you.

182
00:14:33,730 --> 00:14:35,100
Let's meet up instead.

183
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:37,240
I don't check my email much.

184
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:39,010
I'd rather meet in person.

185
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,660
Ms. Lada.

186
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:52,300
When you said

187
00:14:52,450 --> 00:14:54,760
you'd rather meet in person
than read emails,

188
00:14:55,590 --> 00:14:57,480
did you mean just for business?

189
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:01,400
What else did you want me to mean?

190
00:15:18,110 --> 00:15:19,920
Let's just say I'll reply to your emails

191
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:21,600
as quickly as I can.

192
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:28,600
Your lipstick color
looks great on you today.

193
00:15:29,410 --> 00:15:30,440
So pretty.

194
00:15:33,110 --> 00:15:34,110
Thank you.

195
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:36,180
See you then.

196
00:16:27,990 --> 00:16:28,630
What?

197
00:16:28,990 --> 00:16:29,990
What are you looking at?

198
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:32,790
Shouldn't it be me

199
00:16:32,810 --> 00:16:34,890
who's supposed to talk to her?

200
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:38,400
Because of your duty or because she's pretty?

201
00:16:39,210 --> 00:16:40,310
Well, both.

202
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:43,680
Well?

203
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:47,080
Nothing.

204
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:48,810
Well, she came here to discuss

205
00:16:48,830 --> 00:16:51,800
- renovating a house into an office.
- Mm.

206
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:54,030
And... after I’m done with the draft,

207
00:16:54,050 --> 00:16:55,920
I'll send it to you.

208
00:16:56,240 --> 00:16:57,240
You mean the work?

209
00:16:58,590 --> 00:17:00,510
Yes, the work.

210
00:17:00,530 --> 00:17:01,880
What else did you expect?

211
00:17:02,010 --> 00:17:04,400
I thought you were gonna
pass the client to me.

212
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:07,550
But since you two get along this well,

213
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,300
I don't need to step in, huh?

214
00:17:12,380 --> 00:17:13,500
Better get back to work.

215
00:17:19,220 --> 00:17:22,950
Or you can let me talk to her instead.

216
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,390
I'd be happy to.

217
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:25,880
Stay out of this.

218
00:17:26,280 --> 00:17:28,120
Just focus on finishing your own work.

219
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,080
Alright.

220
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:38,440
Xinxin!

221
00:17:39,940 --> 00:17:40,870
Oh?

222
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:44,430
I just saw your new car.

223
00:17:44,450 --> 00:17:45,600
Did you buy it?

224
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:48,020
No, I didn't.

225
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:50,450
He gave it to me.

226
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:52,390
And...

227
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,120
you accepted it?

228
00:17:54,630 --> 00:17:56,000
Why wouldn't I?

229
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:57,780
I'm gonna get my revenge

230
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:59,610
by leaving him broke.

231
00:18:04,550 --> 00:18:06,130
Oh, Lada.

232
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:07,800
- Hm?
- Someone wants to see you.

233
00:18:08,390 --> 00:18:09,500
Who?

234
00:18:13,520 --> 00:18:16,210
Ta-da!

235
00:18:17,810 --> 00:18:19,600
Hi, girls!

236
00:18:19,630 --> 00:18:20,990
Nan!

237
00:18:23,610 --> 00:18:24,550
I missed you.

238
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:25,860
Gosh, girl!

239
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:27,640
You came back and didn't even tell me?

240
00:18:27,660 --> 00:18:29,320
Guess your friends
don't matter anymore, huh?

241
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:31,440
Come on...

242
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,660
I've been busy lately.

243
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:34,890
I was planning to tell you
once I sorted everything out.

244
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:38,080
But Xinxin couldn't contain herself,

245
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,960
so she planned this whole surprise.

246
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:42,310
Surprise?

247
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:46,010
And is your offer to check
the feng shui for my new company

248
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:47,360
part of your plan, too?

249
00:18:47,970 --> 00:18:49,520
I was serious about that.

250
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:52,140
It's a gift to celebrate your return

251
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:53,330
and your new company.

252
00:18:54,300 --> 00:18:55,410
You're the best!

253
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,400
Thank you.

254
00:19:06,590 --> 00:19:08,010
Hello.

255
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,500
Is this Xinxin, the feng shui master?

256
00:19:10,800 --> 00:19:12,700
Yes, I am.

257
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,700
Do you remember me?

258
00:19:15,890 --> 00:19:17,320
Well, you sound familiar.

259
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:18,320
Oh?

260
00:19:18,510 --> 00:19:20,310
Let me give you some hints.

261
00:19:21,010 --> 00:19:23,120
I'm gorgeous,

262
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:24,600
capable, confident,

263
00:19:24,620 --> 00:19:25,900
and I sing beautifully, too.

264
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:26,510
Oh!

265
00:19:26,530 --> 00:19:28,050
My daughter is gorgeous,

266
00:19:28,070 --> 00:19:29,500
capable, confident,

267
00:19:29,690 --> 00:19:31,200
and she's an architect, too.

268
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:32,560
Oh, and most importantly...

269
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:35,720
she's single.

270
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:36,950
Oh?!

271
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:38,350
Auntie Tai!

272
00:19:40,300 --> 00:19:41,390
I'm glad

273
00:19:41,710 --> 00:19:43,480
you still remember me.

274
00:19:43,800 --> 00:19:45,910
Anyway, let me get to the point.

275
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:47,400
Well...

276
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:49,790
right now, I feel like my house

277
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:52,080
is really gloomy.

278
00:19:52,470 --> 00:19:54,510
So, I want you to

279
00:19:54,530 --> 00:19:56,950
be the love of this home.

280
00:19:57,930 --> 00:19:59,410
Be the love in your home?

281
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:00,760
What does that mean?

282
00:20:02,330 --> 00:20:03,200
Uh...

283
00:20:03,270 --> 00:20:05,800
Uh, well, what I mean is...

284
00:20:06,610 --> 00:20:08,880
I want to invite you over to

285
00:20:08,910 --> 00:20:10,400
check the feng shui of the house,

286
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:12,910
boost its love energy,

287
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:15,320
and maybe attract a partner for Soul, too.

288
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:16,910
Uh...

289
00:20:16,930 --> 00:20:18,190
Are you free this evening?

290
00:20:18,210 --> 00:20:19,710
Let's have dinner together.

291
00:20:20,650 --> 00:20:22,700
I already have plans for today.

292
00:20:23,290 --> 00:20:24,600
I'm really sorry about that.

293
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,760
Maybe some other time?

294
00:20:27,310 --> 00:20:28,700
Oh... I see.

295
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:29,690
Oh.

296
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,900
It's alright, there's always next time.

297
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:33,890
Anyway...

298
00:20:33,910 --> 00:20:35,710
thank you so much for thinking about me.

299
00:20:36,510 --> 00:20:37,590
Goodbye.

300
00:20:42,210 --> 00:20:43,210
Who was that?

301
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:44,260
Hm?

302
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:46,300
Don't tell me...

303
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,480
There's something between

304
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,410
a feng shui master and an architect?

305
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,610
Like a cat and a dog,

306
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:56,920
water and fire,

307
00:20:57,010 --> 00:20:59,680
rivals turned lovers.

308
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:02,030
Imagined couples become real couples.

309
00:21:02,390 --> 00:21:03,860
Gosh!

310
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:04,750
Listen!

311
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:06,290
Listen to me, girls!

312
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,510
I'm all ears.

313
00:21:09,120 --> 00:21:11,620
Her mom invited me over for dinner.

314
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,490
She didn't call me herself.

315
00:21:14,660 --> 00:21:15,400
Mm.

316
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:17,310
Trying to win her mom over,

317
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:19,290
