558
00:35:14,820 --> 00:35:15,910
- Let me see.
- Hey!

559
00:35:16,040 --> 00:35:16,840
- Oh?!
- Hey!

560
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:18,220
- See? See?
- Hey... Hey!

561
00:35:18,240 --> 00:35:19,440
What are you doing?!

562
00:35:19,660 --> 00:35:21,120
- I told you.
- Come on!

563
00:35:21,600 --> 00:35:22,910
Hey, you!

564
00:35:22,930 --> 00:35:24,320
I told you it's green. See?

565
00:35:24,490 --> 00:35:25,160
Hey!

566
00:35:27,100 --> 00:35:29,140
Oh my, Xinxin!

567
00:35:29,160 --> 00:35:31,560
What are you two taking off?

568
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:34,200
It's not like that, Grandma.

569
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:37,160
I'm looking at her bra...

570
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:37,970
Hey!

571
00:35:37,990 --> 00:35:39,210
Xinxin!

572
00:35:49,260 --> 00:35:50,460
Here,

573
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:52,410
have a drink.

574
00:35:52,430 --> 00:35:54,000
- Thank you.
- Alright.

575
00:35:55,220 --> 00:35:57,790
This is for my daughter.

576
00:35:57,810 --> 00:35:58,960
Thank you.

577
00:35:59,220 --> 00:36:00,600
What's your name, dear?

578
00:36:01,000 --> 00:36:02,090
It's Soul.

579
00:36:02,110 --> 00:36:03,270
Alright, Soul.

580
00:36:03,290 --> 00:36:05,160
What are you to Xinxin?

581
00:36:05,180 --> 00:36:07,820
- She's...
- I'm asking her, dear.

582
00:36:10,680 --> 00:36:13,320
I'm an architect who's working with...

583
00:36:15,190 --> 00:36:16,160
Xinxin.

584
00:36:16,180 --> 00:36:17,880
An architect...

585
00:36:18,110 --> 00:36:20,490
Oh? Is this the one you...

586
00:36:20,910 --> 00:36:23,120
told me about?

587
00:36:23,140 --> 00:36:24,730
- Mom.
- You said...

588
00:36:24,750 --> 00:36:25,400
Huh?

589
00:36:25,600 --> 00:36:27,480
That she's...

590
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,890
Mom, you're just saying things.

591
00:36:29,910 --> 00:36:31,240
Oh.

592
00:36:31,410 --> 00:36:33,620
At first, when I heard about you,

593
00:36:33,640 --> 00:36:35,180
I thought...

594
00:36:35,400 --> 00:36:36,680
you'd be

595
00:36:36,700 --> 00:36:39,100
strict and outspoken,

596
00:36:39,130 --> 00:36:40,640
but you're not like that at all.

597
00:36:40,660 --> 00:36:42,410
You're even prettier in person,

598
00:36:42,430 --> 00:36:44,720
and you have the sweetest smile.

599
00:36:45,100 --> 00:36:45,810
Uh...

600
00:36:46,190 --> 00:36:48,320
Hey, I think my mom might

601
00:36:48,350 --> 00:36:50,920
have mistaken you for another architect.

602
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:52,280
There are a lot of them.

603
00:36:55,900 --> 00:36:58,410
I thought she was your girlfriend.

604
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:01,000
- Mom!
- Hm?

605
00:37:07,420 --> 00:37:08,520
Have some milk.

606
00:37:08,540 --> 00:37:09,240
Thank you.

607
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:32,040
I don't get it.

608
00:37:32,060 --> 00:37:34,900
Why does everyone
have to think we're dating?!

609
00:37:35,010 --> 00:37:36,410
Like your mom,

610
00:37:36,510 --> 00:37:37,510
my mom

611
00:37:38,110 --> 00:37:39,450
and my friends, too.

612
00:37:39,500 --> 00:37:40,020
Huh?!

613
00:37:40,410 --> 00:37:42,650
You went and told your friends about me?

614
00:37:45,690 --> 00:37:46,690
Hey...

615
00:37:47,100 --> 00:37:48,030
you should head back.

616
00:37:48,410 --> 00:37:50,810
And I'm telling you right now

617
00:37:50,830 --> 00:37:53,120
to stay away from my mom.

618
00:37:54,700 --> 00:37:55,700
Even though...

619
00:37:56,080 --> 00:37:57,930
she seems to like you a lot.

620
00:37:58,000 --> 00:37:58,950
Gosh,

621
00:37:59,220 --> 00:38:00,520
you're acting like a kid.

622
00:38:00,540 --> 00:38:01,910
How old are you, huh?

623
00:38:02,380 --> 00:38:04,010
And how old are you, then?

624
00:38:04,220 --> 00:38:06,040
Hey, I asked you first.

625
00:38:06,800 --> 00:38:08,110
You tell me yours first,

626
00:38:08,130 --> 00:38:09,520
then I'll tell you mine.

627
00:38:09,540 --> 00:38:10,500
It's fair that way.

628
00:38:12,790 --> 00:38:13,920
I'm 29.

629
00:38:15,060 --> 00:38:16,570
- You're old...
- Hey, you!

630
00:38:18,100 --> 00:38:19,860
I'm 25.

631
00:38:21,010 --> 00:38:22,430
You look like you're in your 30s.

632
00:38:23,200 --> 00:38:24,560
That's too much.

633
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:26,010
Just kidding.

634
00:38:28,420 --> 00:38:29,420
With a mouth like that,

635
00:38:29,660 --> 00:38:32,190
you’ll never find a partner
in this lifetime.

636
00:38:32,900 --> 00:38:34,100
With a face like that,

637
00:38:34,130 --> 00:38:35,560
you'll probably be single for life.

638
00:38:35,580 --> 00:38:37,000
Nobody could stand you.

639
00:38:38,310 --> 00:38:40,250
I just don't want anyone yet.

640
00:38:41,590 --> 00:38:43,160
You're still single, then?

641
00:38:45,220 --> 00:38:45,990
Hey...

642
00:38:46,170 --> 00:38:47,280
are you trying to fish for info?

643
00:38:47,940 --> 00:38:49,470
I don't have to do that.

644
00:38:49,490 --> 00:38:51,400
It's obvious no one would hit on you.

645
00:38:54,130 --> 00:38:55,190
You should head back now.

646
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:56,710
Come on, go.

647
00:38:59,750 --> 00:39:02,020
Bye. See you again.

648
00:39:02,760 --> 00:39:03,910
What did you just say?

649
00:39:05,410 --> 00:39:07,010
I said that so I wouldn't jinx it.

650
00:39:10,100 --> 00:39:11,100
Oh...

651
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:12,620
See you again, then.

652
00:39:13,710 --> 00:39:15,120
But I mean it.

653
00:39:15,410 --> 00:39:16,410
I'm being serious.

654
00:40:09,500 --> 00:40:10,500
- Soul!
- Soul!

655
00:40:10,700 --> 00:40:11,910
Whoa, what?

656
00:40:12,310 --> 00:40:13,910
I should've asked you that instead.

657
00:40:14,100 --> 00:40:16,360
I've seen you fiddling
with your phone for a while.

658
00:40:16,380 --> 00:40:17,400
Right.

659
00:40:17,420 --> 00:40:19,670
Is there a problem with Madam Waen?

660
00:40:19,980 --> 00:40:20,980
Please,

661
00:40:21,190 --> 00:40:23,200
don't mention her name here.

662
00:40:23,420 --> 00:40:25,300
It's traumatizing.

663
00:40:29,190 --> 00:40:30,190
Who's that?

664
00:40:30,540 --> 00:40:31,720
"Topknot Kuman."

665
00:40:33,490 --> 00:40:34,500
Keep your nose out of it!

666
00:40:37,310 --> 00:40:38,610
Sh*t! I'm screwed.

667
00:40:42,140 --> 00:40:42,690
Oh?

668
00:40:43,260 --> 00:40:45,400
You wanted to talk to me,
but you just called and hung up?

669
00:40:57,100 --> 00:40:58,420
You two, leave for now.

670
00:40:59,010 --> 00:40:59,690
But we're about to...

671
00:40:59,710 --> 00:41:01,370
That can wait. Leave for now.

672
00:41:01,390 --> 00:41:02,000
Me, too?

673
00:41:02,020 --> 00:41:02,790
Yeah!

674
00:41:02,810 --> 00:41:04,470
- Huh?
- What?

675
00:41:04,490 --> 00:41:05,100
Hey.

676
00:41:06,180 --> 00:41:07,590
Leave, both of you.

677
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:08,500
Alright.

678
00:41:10,210 --> 00:41:11,510
Okay.

679
00:41:11,850 --> 00:41:14,100
- And when should I...
- Leave, Oyl.

680
00:41:14,120 --> 00:41:14,920
Understood.

681
00:41:15,600 --> 00:41:16,950
Come on, let's go.

682
00:41:21,300 --> 00:41:22,300
Hello.

683
00:41:23,100 --> 00:41:24,100
Miss Architect.

684
00:41:24,120 --> 00:41:26,010
You wanted to talk to me,
but you just called and hung up?

685
00:41:26,030 --> 00:41:28,210
Times have changed, Miss.

686
00:41:28,240 --> 00:41:30,470
No one uses prepaid phone cards

687
00:41:30,490 --> 00:41:31,720
and worries about
using up their credit by calling.

688
00:41:31,740 --> 00:41:35,340
These days, even monthly plans
let you prepay by the hour.

689
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:36,900
What era were you born in, huh?

690
00:41:38,220 --> 00:41:38,910
Hey.

691
00:41:39,700 --> 00:41:40,610
My finger slipped.

692
00:41:41,940 --> 00:41:42,610
What?

693
00:41:42,970 --> 00:41:44,960
So I'm wasting my time calling you back?

694
00:41:46,210 --> 00:41:47,590
Are you free right now?

695
00:41:48,290 --> 00:41:50,040
I'll make it worth your time.

696
00:41:51,120 --> 00:41:52,110
What now?

697
00:41:53,420 --> 00:41:54,140
Well...

698
00:41:54,700 --> 00:41:57,000
I want to discuss
Mr. Mongkol's project with you.

699
00:42:00,620 --> 00:42:02,090
I'm free.

700
00:42:02,300 --> 00:42:03,810
I just finished work, actually.

701
00:42:04,350 --> 00:42:05,910
But...

702
00:42:05,930 --> 00:42:07,910
I still can't find a ride home.

703
00:42:08,090 --> 00:42:09,490
Are you free, Miss Architect?

704
00:42:09,950 --> 00:42:11,000
Can you come pick me up?

705
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:12,820
Where?

706
00:42:13,700 --> 00:42:14,900
Pathum Thani.

707
00:42:25,010 --> 00:42:26,890
Hello, Miss Architect.

708
00:42:27,090 --> 00:42:28,280
We meet again.

709
00:42:28,850 --> 00:42:31,390
Didn't you say
you were just trying not to jinx it?

710
00:42:31,410 --> 00:42:33,290
Then why do we have to meet again today?

711
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:36,840
I didn't think
you'd actually come pick me up.

712
00:42:37,210 --> 00:42:38,800
You're lucky

713
00:42:38,820 --> 00:42:40,400
I happen to work around here.

714
00:42:42,400 --> 00:42:44,310
I guess I really am lucky.

715
00:42:44,330 --> 00:42:45,330
Because...

716
00:42:45,610 --> 00:42:47,310
I haven't even called a ride yet,

717
00:42:48,010 --> 00:42:49,700
and my chariot's already here.

718
00:42:50,070 --> 00:42:51,560
Did you trick me?

719
00:42:54,560 --> 00:42:55,800
What are you waiting for?

720
00:42:55,820 --> 00:42:56,820
Why not get in?

721
00:42:58,290 --> 00:43:00,420
Waiting for the invitation, I guess?

722
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:02,800
Get in.

723
00:43:12,620 --> 00:43:14,920
Where are you taking me?

724
00:43:16,510 --> 00:43:17,900
You'll see.

725
00:43:20,300 --> 00:43:21,890
Do you like to surprise people?

726
00:43:25,180 --> 00:43:26,180
Well, a little.

727
00:43:42,440 --> 00:43:43,500
Hey!

728
00:43:44,870 --> 00:43:46,830
Did you trick me into
coming to your house again?

729
00:43:47,350 --> 00:43:48,440
What did I do?

730
00:43:48,460 --> 00:43:49,750
You were the one who hopped in,

731
00:43:49,770 --> 00:43:50,550
don't you remember?

732
00:43:51,930 --> 00:43:54,070
You really are a lioness.

733
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:55,710
Hey,

734
00:43:55,730 --> 00:43:56,620
don't be dramatic.

735
00:43:56,640 --> 00:43:57,940
My mom's here, too.

736
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:59,300
And most importantly,

737
00:43:59,390 --> 00:44:01,300
I don't like you that much.

738
00:44:04,090 --> 00:44:06,300
I don't like you that much either.

739
00:44:13,210 --> 00:44:14,510
I'm back, Mom.

740
00:44:16,050 --> 00:44:17,380
Xinxin, dear.

741
00:44:18,900 --> 00:44:20,600
Hello, Auntie.

742
00:44:20,940 --> 00:44:22,100
How did you get here?

743
00:44:22,430 --> 00:44:23,090
Oh.

744
00:44:23,320 --> 00:44:25,960
Ms. Soul picked me up to discuss work.

745
00:44:26,050 --> 00:44:27,510
Hm...

746
00:44:27,970 --> 00:44:29,570
She picked you up?

747
00:44:30,730 --> 00:44:33,000
I just happened to be
around there for work, Mom.

748
00:44:34,290 --> 00:44:36,710
But I thought you said
you'd be in the office all day.

749
00:44:38,060 --> 00:44:40,500
I'll go upstairs to discuss work, Mom.

750
00:44:40,710 --> 00:44:41,680
Come on, let's go.

751
00:44:41,820 --> 00:44:43,500
I'll be going now, Auntie.

752
00:44:58,190 --> 00:44:59,780
I just don't want her to bother us.

753
00:44:59,810 --> 00:45:01,510
Don't mind her.

754
00:45:01,690 --> 00:45:02,690
I see...

755
00:45:03,290 --> 00:45:04,820
This applies to you too, then.

756
00:45:05,440 --> 00:45:05,900
Huh?

757
00:45:06,640 --> 00:45:08,390
Don't mind my mom, either.

758
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:09,790
Gosh...

759
00:45:09,810 --> 00:45:12,210
I'm totally fine with it. Don't worry.

760
00:45:12,420 --> 00:45:14,280
Sit and wait here.

761
00:45:14,310 --> 00:45:15,710
I'll go get some snacks for you.

762
00:45:46,170 --> 00:45:47,170
What are you up to?

763
00:45:50,390 --> 00:45:52,070
You talk as if I'm a child.

764
00:45:54,100 --> 00:45:56,880
I was just checking
your desk's feng shui for you.

765
00:45:58,500 --> 00:45:59,500
So, how is it?

766
00:46:02,000 --> 00:46:03,000
It's good.

767
00:46:03,420 --> 00:46:04,190
But...

768
00:46:04,390 --> 00:46:05,450
one thing's missing.

769
00:46:06,060 --> 00:46:07,320
A plant on your desk.

770
00:46:07,750 --> 00:46:09,800
Without a touch of green, your ideas get stuck

771
00:46:09,820 --> 00:46:11,290
and you lose motivation.

772
00:46:11,710 --> 00:46:14,790
You want me to grow a plant on my desk?

773
00:46:15,700 --> 00:46:17,930
I mean a small one.

774
00:46:18,230 --> 00:46:19,810
Like a golden pothos or something.

775
00:46:20,310 --> 00:46:23,210
Who on earth
puts a tree on their desk?

776
00:46:24,220 --> 00:46:25,220
You're not exactly normal,

777
00:46:25,680 --> 00:46:26,950
you know.

778
00:46:27,900 --> 00:46:28,990
Miss Architect.

779
00:46:34,110 --> 00:46:35,490
And...

780
00:46:35,520 --> 00:46:36,590
one more thing,

781
00:46:36,790 --> 00:46:38,850
the number of lights in your room is odd

782
00:46:38,920 --> 00:46:40,900
when it should be even.

783
00:46:40,920 --> 00:46:43,260
- So you...
- "Won't be unlucky in love."

784
00:46:44,110 --> 00:46:44,920
Am I right?

785
00:46:46,810 --> 00:46:47,810
Mm.

786
00:46:49,410 --> 00:46:51,030
If it's too much for you,

787
00:46:51,050 --> 00:46:53,730
you can just get a desk lamp.

788
00:46:54,200 --> 00:46:55,200
Why?

789
00:46:55,870 --> 00:46:58,600
It'll bring you luck in love.

790
00:47:09,990 --> 00:47:11,190
Can you guarantee that?

791
00:47:12,200 --> 00:47:14,400
You have my word as Xinxin,
the feng shui master.

792
00:47:25,700 --> 00:47:26,980
I'll buy it for you.

793
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:29,320
Consider it a good-luck charm
from a feng shui master.

794
00:47:29,420 --> 00:47:30,230
I don't want it.

795
00:47:30,410 --> 00:47:32,530
It's not like I want
to be in love that much anyway.

796
00:47:32,990 --> 00:47:34,440
It wouldn't hurt, you know.

797
00:47:34,600 --> 00:47:35,720
I'm free today,

798
00:47:35,920 --> 00:47:38,100
and my whole day is yours.

799
00:47:38,290 --> 00:47:39,190
Are you sure it will work?

800
00:47:39,200 --> 00:47:40,990
If the client doesn't like it,

801
00:47:41,200 --> 00:47:42,410
we'll all be in trouble.

802
00:47:42,840 --> 00:47:44,820
Can you stop sticking your nose in?!

803
00:47:44,910 --> 00:47:47,010
This is how the real world works!

804
00:47:51,100 --> 00:47:53,410
You're almost 30, dear.

805
00:47:54,700 --> 00:47:56,880
Just 30, Mom.

806
00:47:56,900 --> 00:47:58,990
If I'm still single at 40,

807
00:47:59,160 --> 00:48:00,530
then you can worry.

808
00:48:02,300 --> 00:48:04,000
But this girl

809
00:48:04,610 --> 00:48:06,200
is cute, though.

810
00:48:06,220 --> 00:48:07,360
I approve.

811
00:48:07,800 --> 00:48:09,720
But we don't know
if she's still single or not.

812
00:48:09,750 --> 00:48:10,810
We'd better get the info first.

813
00:48:10,840 --> 00:48:12,200
What are you saying, Mom?

814
00:48:12,290 --> 00:48:13,820
We just met.

815
00:48:14,020 --> 00:48:15,500
How can you approve of her?

816
00:48:16,290 --> 00:48:18,840
Well, it just felt right.

817
00:48:19,010 --> 00:48:19,910
Oh?

818
00:48:20,370 --> 00:48:21,300
Should I...

819
00:48:21,800 --> 00:48:23,410
reach out to the official page directly?

820
00:48:23,510 --> 00:48:26,660
Hey, don't do that! It's embarrassing!

821
00:48:26,790 --> 00:48:27,830
Please don't, I'm begging you.

822
00:48:27,850 --> 00:48:29,000
Don't do something like that.

823
00:48:29,200 --> 00:48:30,290
Let me tell you,

824
00:48:30,510 --> 00:48:33,320
the days of waiting for someone
to confess their love are over.

825
00:48:33,340 --> 00:48:35,110
Should I love her, or should I not?

826
00:48:35,440 --> 00:48:36,440
That won't do.

827
00:48:36,610 --> 00:48:37,800
You've got to make a move,

828
00:48:37,820 --> 00:48:38,500
get her info,

829
00:48:38,520 --> 00:48:39,050
and find out

830
00:48:39,070 --> 00:48:40,680
if she's taken.

831
00:48:42,200 --> 00:48:43,310
And if she's single,

832
00:48:43,800 --> 00:48:44,960
seal the deal for me, okay?

833
00:48:46,020 --> 00:48:47,020
Mom...

834
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:50,620
I'm serious.

835
00:48:54,100 --> 00:48:55,100
Soul.

836
00:48:56,810 --> 00:48:59,220
How long are you going
to keep shutting yourself off?

837
00:49:01,300 --> 00:49:02,810
Does one heartbreak

838
00:49:03,990 --> 00:49:06,690
really make you scared to love again?

839
00:49:17,920 --> 00:49:19,400
Give it a chance.
